// Resonance3D - Xbox menu palette (XM.1 item 13 step 2).
//
// Content only: this file is staged onto Xbox discs alone
// (tools/xbox-xiso.sh), so it changes nothing for any other platform,
// and nothing changes here if this file is ever missing - mainui's own
// UI_ApplyCustomColors treats an absent colors.lst as normal, not an
// error, and every value it can set already has a stock default.
//
// Two roles moved to the design canvas's amber; a third is deliberately
// left alone. HEADING_COLOR is a key this fork added (BaseMenu.h/.cpp) -
// stock mainui has no colour role for a screen heading at all, so every
// Xbox heading reused HELP_COLOR by default until this file's own
// sibling code change gave it one. PROMPT_TEXT_COLOR/PROMPT_FOCUS_COLOR
// are stock keys already read by every CMenuBaseItem-derived control
// (BaseItem.cpp:65-66) - the WON-style text rows this fork's own text
// buttons render through (PicButton.cpp:354-379) pick these up directly,
// so Main's, Options', Game's and Audio's row labels go from stock
// amber-ish base / pure yellow focus to the canvas's dim-to-bright amber
// with no code change at all.
//
// HELP_COLOR is NOT set here, on purpose, not an oversight: it is one
// global shared by two roles the canvas draws differently - a slider's
// or checkbox's own label (Slider.cpp:165/206, CheckBox.cpp:48, the
// canvas's tan/bone .lbl) and a screen's status/help line
// (PicButton.cpp:252, the canvas's blue-grey .hint). Setting it to
// either colour would get the other role wrong. Untangling that needs
// a second new colour role, the same shape as HEADING_COLOR above, and
// is a tracked follow-up, not guessed here.

HEADING_COLOR
255 176 32

PROMPT_TEXT_COLOR
200 134 28

PROMPT_FOCUS_COLOR
255 176 32
